  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A test fails on origin/master: with more empty-lookup Signals than one run's bound, two (or N) successive runs together read and redact every deleted code's Signals, including codes that sort past the first run's bound.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must-not-fire: a cursor that is missing or unreadable restarts from the beginning (no rows skipped); a run under the bound behaves exactly as today; Signals of existing policies are untouched; already-redacted evidence is not rewritten; existing SignalClosure, SignalReevaluation and redaction tests pass unmodified (or a changed assertion is justified in the PR).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reaching the bound is reported with counts and no longer marks a progressing run failed (test); build, filtered tests (Signals) and full ArchTests pass; publish-size delta reported.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>The fix needs a schema change, a new service or DI registration beyond an existing cache/store, changes which evidence is redacted, or would skip rows when the cursor is lost: STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <execution>
    <protocol>Run through task-execute. Fresh branch from origin/master in a short-path worktree (C:\wt224); PR to master; do not merge.</protocol>
  </execution>
  <completion>Done 2026-11-25: PR #3164 squash-merged to master (ef1dc4f2c9), closes #2085 (DI-116). Option (a): SignalClosureService.DeletedPolicyCodesWithSignalsAsync takes an optional sprk_signalid cursor (GreaterThan, same order, paging and bound) and returns SignalsRead and ResumeAfter; SignalReevaluationJob keeps the cursor in the existing IDistributedCache (key sprk:ontology:evaluator:deleted-policy-redaction-cursor, 7-day TTL, same shape as TodoAssigneeOwnerReconciliationJob), saves it after the sweep when the bound is reached, clears it at the end of a pass, and starts from the beginning when it is missing, unreadable or the cache read faults. Reaching the bound logs a Warning with counts and no longer fails the run; the run fails only if the cursor cannot be saved or cleared. Redaction rule, D-61 and one-failure-per-policy accounting unchanged; no schema or DI change. Tests: 8 new (10 cases) incl. a three-run must-fire that fails on master; the fake pages the empty-policy read in SqlGuid order (a .NET-max cursor mutation fails 2 tests); one R4 assertion pair changed per AC3. Signals filter 5,530 pass; full ArchTests 2,831 pass; publish size +3,580 bytes. Independent Opus adversarial review: merge, no F-class; known limits recorded in notes/task-224-notes.md (per-pass rather than nightly re-check of early codes; nightly cache eviction would stall with only a Warning; save-after-sweep not pinned by a test). The per-code MaxPages throw in ReadPolicySignalsAsync predates this task: filed as #3170 (DI-176). Dev check: the first 02:30Z re-evaluation run after the next dev BFF build. Dev check 2026-11-26 02:30Z on dev BFF 1e64e94168 (first run with the cursor): PASS. The run Succeeded (164 items, 43.7 s) with no bound Warning, so the pass completed and the cursor was cleared.</completion>
</task>
